  "actualResult": "The original full-body export was rejected after visual QA exposed hidden helper geometry. A clean head-neck-and-eyes-only solve package was rebuilt, normalized, measured and rendered at 1440x2560 from five fixed views; it remains only an input for a future MetaHuman Identity solve. A reproducible MediaPipe landmark baseline against canonical image 03 measured the principal front-view identity deltas without fabricating an identity score. Canonical profiles 07/08 were detector-valid, but both candidate profiles failed detection; automated profile scoring therefore failed closed and a human-reviewed comparison board defines conform constraints. An Editor-only UE 5.6 deformation QA contract now covers 15 cases and 11 defect classes under the Looking Glass Go profile; runtime verification remains explicitly pending. Canonical body reference 16 and the v79 Go render produced stable pose landmarks; the baseline shows shoulder width is close while torso length, not absolute leg length, is the primary proportion mismatch. Human-reviewed source evidence now establishes neutral, smile and mouth-open expression anchors, raising truthful expression coverage from 0/16 to 3/16; the other 13 states remain explicitly missing and no viseme labels were inferred. A null-by-default MetaHuman candidate binding, read-only UE 5.6 asset collector and post-conform gate now require real Identity, mesh, rig, Groom, DNA/RigLogic and five immutable Go renders; fixture evidence passes while the current workspace correctly remains pending. A separate production surface gate now rejects the diffuse-only v79 skin and prototype eyes unless a real 4K eight-channel skin set, eight facial zones, six physical eye parts, Editor bindings and seven immutable Go close-ups exist. A production Groom gate similarly rejects the dense generic Hair Editor blockout until canonical grouping and styling, real Unreal Groom/scalp bindings, strands plus fallback LOD, runtime collision checks and fourteen immutable Go captures exist. A modular clothing gate preserves the valuable body/garment separation but rejects the procedural v79 outfit until patterned PBR assets, Chaos Cloth/Dataflow, body-independent swapping, LODs, zero-penetration runtime checks and sixteen immutable Go captures exist. A frame-level deformation evaluator now requires eleven unit-bound geometry diagnostics at all forty-five declared samples, rejecting missing, duplicate, non-finite, threshold-exceeding or self-inconsistent evidence before G4 review. The evidence scorecard reports three measured-but-unscored components, ten unverified components and eleven blocking defects; overall remains null instead of presenting a fabricated AAA percentage. A deterministic refinement decision engine registers v001 as the baseline and will only keep future iterations when target metrics improve without guardrail regression or blocking defects; unscored comparisons remain inconclusive. A fail-closed TRELLIS.2/Hunyuan3D benchmark now requires six equally seeded, fully attributable temporary shape candidates with cleanup, measurements and nine fixed Looking Glass Go renders each; the workspace truthfully remains at zero candidates until both pinned toolchains and reviewed weights are available.",
